    "summary": "Hartford ’82 delivers a high‑energy blaze with Let It Grow fireworks & Phil’s earthquake space.",
    "review": "April 18, 1982 at the Hartford Civic Center is one of those shows that feels like pure momentum from the first note to the final encore. The band launches into a smoking “Bertha” and rolls straight through a tight first set packed with a ripping “Let It Grow,” soaring “Space,” and a thunder‑ous “Big Railroad Blues.”  But it’s the second set where the magic really unfolds – a seamless cascade of “Playing In The Band → Eyes Of The World → Phil’s Earthquake Space → The Other One → Black Peter” that builds into an ecstatic climax before the final “Sunshine Daydream.”  Across every source, Jerry’s lead work is described as “amazing,” especially his incendiary solo on “Let It Grow,” while Phil’s bass underpins a spaced‑out, quake‑like space jam that shakes the venue.  Brent Mydland’s organ adds a slashing, church‑organ texture to the bluesier moments, and the Rhythm Devils drive each peak with relentless energy.  The Miller soundboard (gd82-04-18.sbd.miller…) captures all of this in crystal‑clear balance, making it the definitive listening choice, though excellent audience tapes and a solid matrix mix also convey the show’s fire.",
